<title>USA: GOLF-FINAL SCORES FROM PGA SPRINT INTERNATIONAL.</title>
<headline>GOLF-FINAL SCORES FROM PGA SPRINT INTERNATIONAL.</headline>
<dateline>CASTLE ROCK, Colorado 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scores after the</p>
<p>final round of the $1.7 million Sprint International golf</p>
<p>tournament won by Phil Mickelson on Sunday</p>
<p>Scoring according to Modified Stableford format, which</p>
<p>awards five points for eagle, two for birdie, zero for par,</p>
<p>and subtracts one point for bogey and three points for double</p>
<p>bogey or worse (Players U.S. unless noted):</p>
<p>48 points - Phil Mickelson 14 13 12 9</p>
<p>41 - Stuart Appleby (Australia) 9 10 13 9</p>
<p>38 - Skip Kendall 10 12 12 4</p>
<p>34 - Dudley Hart 10 10 8 6</p>
<p>33 - Kevin Sutherland 3 14 8 8, Jay Haas 15 4 10 4</p>
<p>32 - Jim Furyk 3 8 12 9, Ernie Els (South Africa) 5 6 14 7,</p>
<p>Larry Mize 15 8 3 6</p>
<p>31 - Nick Price (Zimbabwe) 6 14 7 4</p>
<p>30 - Scott McCarron 11 13 2 4</p>
<p>29 - Davis Love 5 8 9 7</p>
<p>28 - Neal Lancaster 8 14 5 1</p>
<p>27 - Andrew Magee 11 5 8 3</p>
<p>26 - Hideki Kase (Japan) 10 2 12 2</p>
<p>25 - Brad Faxon 10 8 3 4, Pete Jordan 6 11 6 2</p>
<p>23 - Kenny Perry 9 6 7 1, Steve Stricker 7 9 7 0, Kirk</p>
<p>Triplett 8 10 6 -1</p>
<p>22 - Tom Purtzer -4 20 7 -1</p>
<p>20 - Brent Geiberger 8 2 13 -3</p>
<p>17 - David Sutherland 3 9 12 -7</p>
<p>14 - Tommy Armour 8 8 11 -13</p>
</text>
